.factory-watermark
.claude/traces/

# Instance configs are yours: they name real repos and hosts, and they belong
# to the machine that runs them rather than to the repo. example.toml is the
# documented template and ships; `./factory init` writes the rest.
# Back them up outside the repo — a fresh clone cannot restore them.
factories/*.toml
!factories/example.toml

# The picker is a Go binary built from source by ./factory (cmd/factory).
bin/

# identity/<role> hooks resolve credentials (contracts/extending.md). Whatever a
# build drops here stays on the machine — a token that reaches a commit is a
# token you have to rotate. The README documenting the hook is the exception.
identity/*
!identity/README.md

# runtimes/<name>.sh is the other drop-in seam (contracts/extending.md §1). This
# build ships none: `resident` and `one-shot` resolve to scripts in the repo
# root, and anything else is a file somebody else's build put here.
runtimes/*
!runtimes/README.md

# Release tarballs, built by .github/build-release.sh.
dist/
